WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.473 --> 00:00:01.806
- Looks so good.

00:00:06.648 --> 00:00:09.200
I have this scar that I got
when I was three years old.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.451
My aunt was taking care of
me at the time and instead of

00:00:12.451 --> 00:00:14.925
sitting me down in a high
chair like a normal three year

00:00:14.925 --> 00:00:18.110
old kid I was sat down in a regular chair.

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:21.506
She served me this bowl of soup
and for a second she turned

00:00:21.506 --> 00:00:25.500
around and I poured the
hot bowl of soup on myself.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:26.917
Covering my chest,

00:00:26.917 --> 00:00:28.009
my right arm,

00:00:28.009 --> 00:00:29.222
and my right leg.

00:00:29.222 --> 00:00:30.692
I had third degree burns and I still have

00:00:30.692 --> 00:00:32.462
the scar on my chest.

00:00:32.462 --> 00:00:34.546
- I have a scar here that I got from

00:00:34.546 --> 00:00:36.230
playing basketball last year.

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:37.524
It was a freak accident.

00:00:37.524 --> 00:00:40.212
I got tripped up and
when I woke up I saw my

00:00:40.212 --> 00:00:42.544
knee cap lodged in my thigh.

00:00:42.544 --> 00:00:43.409
I called my mom.

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:44.681
She rushed me to the ER.

00:00:44.681 --> 00:00:46.865
The doctor basically said that I had

00:00:46.865 --> 00:00:48.505
a ruptured patella tendon.

00:00:48.505 --> 00:00:51.938
This tendon from my
knee cap to my shin bone

00:00:51.938 --> 00:00:53.793
had ruptured and exploded.

00:00:53.793 --> 00:00:56.493
There was nothing keeping
these two things connected so

00:00:56.493 --> 00:00:58.945
basically my leg would go limp.

00:00:58.945 --> 00:00:59.856
Kind of like that.

00:00:59.856 --> 00:01:01.812
So we're here at The Warren Tattoo to.

00:01:01.812 --> 00:01:03.827
[Oscar] Get a tattoo to cover up my scar.

00:01:03.827 --> 00:01:06.509
- So you're wanting to
incorporate your scar like not

00:01:06.509 --> 00:01:07.934
actually cover it all
but sort of decorate?

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:10.386
- Yeah I definitely don't want
to cover it up just because

00:01:10.386 --> 00:01:11.431
it's been with me my whole life.

00:01:11.431 --> 00:01:15.598
But I do want something on it
to kind of bring it together.

00:01:17.532 --> 00:01:20.591
I'm like very Mexican and so
I want something to do with my

00:01:20.591 --> 00:01:23.393
background and so I'm obsessed
with the Dia de los Muertos.

00:01:23.393 --> 00:01:25.595
Both the skulls and the flowers.

00:01:25.595 --> 00:01:29.389
I do want a quote probably
somewhere around here or here.

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:32.112
She actually has a flower tattoo as well.

00:01:32.112 --> 00:01:34.283
It was kind of like when she
went through depression too.

00:01:34.283 --> 00:01:37.229
You know, I just kind of want
to get the same flower here.

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:40.358
- Do you want that to be
actually connecting to your scar?

00:01:40.358 --> 00:01:43.028
- [Victor] Yeah. The scar's like the stem.

00:01:43.028 --> 00:01:45.080
(lively music)

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:46.360
- [Oscar] I'm nervous
but I'm kind of excited.

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:47.193
- Yep.

00:01:47.193 --> 00:01:49.426
(buzzing)

00:01:49.426 --> 00:01:50.394
- That noise.

00:01:50.394 --> 00:01:51.475
(laughs)

00:01:51.475 --> 00:01:53.727
- [Oscar's Mom] When
I walk into the house,

00:01:53.727 --> 00:01:55.784
the first thing I saw was
he was very red and he had

00:01:55.784 --> 00:01:57.166
blisters on his chest.

00:01:57.166 --> 00:01:58.779
I rushed him to the hospital.

00:01:58.779 --> 00:02:00.914
They had told me to put him
on the hospital bed and he was

00:02:00.914 --> 00:02:03.636
crying and screaming and he
keep holding onto me and saying

00:02:03.636 --> 00:02:05.088
no mommy, please no.

00:02:05.088 --> 00:02:05.921
So, I.

00:02:08.649 --> 00:02:09.482
- Aww.

00:02:11.117 --> 00:02:12.714
(crying)

00:02:12.714 --> 00:02:14.357
You're gonna make me cry too mom.

00:02:14.357 --> 00:02:18.116
- It's because it's so sad
to see your son crying and

00:02:18.116 --> 00:02:19.928
screaming and you feel,

00:02:19.928 --> 00:02:23.058
you can't do nothing about it.

00:02:23.058 --> 00:02:25.475
(soft music)

00:02:28.625 --> 00:02:30.359
- This is for you ma.

00:02:30.359 --> 00:02:31.192
- [Artist] Ready?

00:02:31.192 --> 00:02:32.025
- Yeah let's do this.

00:02:32.025 --> 00:02:32.858
(buzzing)

00:02:32.858 --> 00:02:34.550
- [Victor] I'm nervous.

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:35.978
(buzzing)

00:02:35.978 --> 00:02:38.418
- [Victor's Mom] I saw
him sat down on the floor,

00:02:38.418 --> 00:02:40.489
very painful that walk cannot straight.

00:02:40.489 --> 00:02:42.917
You hurt your body but you
also hurt in your heart.

00:02:42.917 --> 00:02:44.717
And you cannot share that pain.

00:02:44.717 --> 00:02:46.574
You really want to take a little bit pain

00:02:46.574 --> 00:02:48.229
from that person to you.

00:02:48.229 --> 00:02:49.062
To share that.

00:02:49.062 --> 00:02:50.491
The only thing I can tell him that.

00:02:50.491 --> 00:02:51.694
To be where you are.

00:02:51.694 --> 00:02:53.823
I always believe if anything happens,

00:02:53.823 --> 00:02:54.968
it could be worse.

00:02:54.968 --> 00:02:55.801
(buzzing)

00:02:55.801 --> 00:02:56.634
- How are you feeling so far?

00:02:56.634 --> 00:02:57.467
- Good.

00:02:57.467 --> 00:02:59.434
It's always like that first initial pinch.

00:02:59.434 --> 00:03:01.256
So growing up,

00:03:01.256 --> 00:03:04.259
middle school was a tough three years.

00:03:04.259 --> 00:03:05.339
Everybody has PE.

00:03:05.339 --> 00:03:06.384
We have to change.

00:03:06.384 --> 00:03:10.064
I was embarrassed of showing
my scars so I would either

00:03:10.064 --> 00:03:12.885
change in the bathroom before
going into the locker room

00:03:12.885 --> 00:03:16.163
or I would the shirt underneath
and then just go to school

00:03:16.163 --> 00:03:17.831
dressed in my PE shirt.

00:03:17.831 --> 00:03:20.901
I feel like that's always
something I've had to deal with.

00:03:20.901 --> 00:03:23.131
As an adult I got a little bit
better about it but I'm still

00:03:23.131 --> 00:03:26.237
shy sometimes when it comes
to like taking off my shirt

00:03:26.237 --> 00:03:27.739
and showing my scar.

00:03:27.739 --> 00:03:29.906
(buzzing)

00:03:31.576 --> 00:03:34.164
- I went through a lot mentally
and obviously physically.

00:03:34.164 --> 00:03:36.075
Couldn't walk for three months.

00:03:36.075 --> 00:03:39.059
The surgery recovery itself
was one of the most painful

00:03:39.059 --> 00:03:40.647
things I've experienced in my life.

00:03:40.647 --> 00:03:43.997
To this day I still remember
every single ticking point

00:03:43.997 --> 00:03:46.923
that changed me internally
and made me appreciate

00:03:46.923 --> 00:03:47.958
the small things in life.

00:03:47.958 --> 00:03:50.245
Realize that you can't take
any little thing for granted

00:03:50.245 --> 00:03:53.095
like walking or even bending
your knee and how important

00:03:53.095 --> 00:03:55.473
that is to your every day life was a very

00:03:55.473 --> 00:03:56.373
tough moment for me.

00:03:56.373 --> 00:03:58.847
And this scar is a daily
reminder of the pain that I felt

00:03:58.847 --> 00:04:00.513
then and the pain that I feel now.

00:04:00.513 --> 00:04:03.461
(uplifting music)

00:04:03.461 --> 00:04:04.796
- Can I see, can I see?

00:04:04.796 --> 00:04:06.104
(gasp)

00:04:06.104 --> 00:04:06.937
Wow.

00:04:08.146 --> 00:04:10.336
[Victor]- This is it.

00:04:10.336 --> 00:04:11.169
- [Victor's Mom] Wow.

00:04:11.169 --> 00:04:12.336
- [Victor] Yeah, it was a little painful

00:04:12.336 --> 00:04:14.236
but not as painful as what I went through.

00:04:14.236 --> 00:04:16.430
- I probably won't be taking
my shirt off anytime soon but

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:19.030
I am comfortable now that
I have a tattoo to show.

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:22.415
- So this is my way of saying
thank you for everything.

00:04:22.415 --> 00:04:23.248
(sniffs)

00:04:23.248 --> 00:04:24.846
For taking care of me
and literally helping me

00:04:24.846 --> 00:04:25.946
stand back up.

00:04:25.946 --> 00:04:28.343
- I will forever have the scar
and now it's kind of cool to

00:04:28.343 --> 00:04:30.851
like have a tattoo on it that I will have

00:04:30.851 --> 00:04:31.785
for the rest of my life.

00:04:31.785 --> 00:04:33.282
- When I look back at this tattoo.

00:04:33.282 --> 00:04:34.206
It's no longer a scar,

00:04:34.206 --> 00:04:36.546
it's a piece of me and a piece of you ma.

00:04:36.546 --> 00:04:38.031
- My heart in there.

00:04:38.031 --> 00:04:39.187
My heart in that little rose.

00:04:39.187 --> 00:04:40.451
- Yeah.

00:04:40.451 --> 00:04:41.329
- Thanks mom for coming.

00:04:41.329 --> 00:04:42.430
(kiss)

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:43.263
- I love you too son.

00:04:43.263 --> 00:04:45.749
(chuckles)

00:04:45.749 --> 00:04:47.504
- I couldn't have done this without you.

00:04:47.504 --> 00:04:49.921
(soft music)

